docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:290:- Correlation: `pair_rail_codex_unavailable` events + `pair_rail_case_emit case=F` + `dispatcher_route_emit reason_code=predicate_codex_outage_5min_fired` should monotonically follow each other on a real outage. Out-of-order = attack signal.
docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:324:**Residual risk:** A novel canonical path added between corpus runs creates a gap window. Mitigation: `test_deny_list_coverage_vs_canonical_guards()` runs in CI on every commit; any canonical-path addition that skips deny-list update fails the test gate (blocks merge).
docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:352:4. **`check_pair_rail.py` verify-then-invoke at EVERY Codex invocation** ✅ **SHIPPED ADR-182** (supersedes the former `codex.py` TOCTOU-heuristic intent) — `_resolve_codex_bin()` mirrors the launcher's `findCodexExecutable()` to resolve the native payload, computes its SHA-256, compares against the manifest entry, and returns the verified absolute path; `_invoke_codex_review()` execs EXACTLY that path (never `codex` re-resolved from `$PATH`, never the launcher). Mismatch / triple-absent → fail-CLOSED `{decision: block}` (`pair_rail_codex_pin_mismatch` audit); manifest-unreadable / payload-missing → INFRA fail-OPEN advisory per the hook's standing doctrine. This closes the PATH-decoy, package-upgrade, and launcher-indirection arms of T-8 at the call site, and narrows the symlink-pivot TOCTOU to the hash→exec window on one already-resolved absolute path.
docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:507:- ADR-108 reopen criterion: any deny-list bypass finding in `danger-full-access` mode triggers immediate pair-rail demotion to advisory + Owner incident response.
