.claude/plans/PLAN-162/ceremony-2-staged/amend2-pair-rail.patch:841:+| `pair_rail_case` (v2.23) | `action`, `case` (str — closed enum: `A` / `B` / `C` / `D` / `E` / `F` per spec.md §11 asymmetric matrix), `claude_verdict` (str — closed enum: `PASS` / `BLOCK`), `codex_verdict` (str — closed enum: `PASS` / `BLOCK` / `ADVISORY` / `TIMEOUT` / `MALFORMED`), `tool_name` (str ≤32 — closed enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty) PER-INVOCATION correlation id, PLAN-161 W2 C5 r5 F2: minted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at review entry (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and IDENTICAL on this case emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_review_expected` — the invocation correlation key the /ceo-boot `failopen_rail_liveness_7d` expected/terminal pairing matches on; off-shape COERCED to empty in the typed wrapper AND the `emit_generic` dispatch branch (r6 F2: the RAW value is validated — any other length incl. oversize, uppercase or non-hex is DROPPED, never truncated, so two distinct off-shape ids sharing a 16-hex prefix can never alias to one pairing key); empty = legacy/id-less emit, paired via the (session, file-hash) bucket-count fallback), `precondition_met` (bool — Case-B requires file:line cited + rubric_violation_id ∈ catalogue + severity ∈ {P0, P1}), `rubric_violation_id` (str ≤64 — enumerated ID from `.claude/policies/rubric-violation-catalogue.yaml` or empty when not Case-B; free-form rubric IDs are sanitized to `unknown_rubric_id`), `severity` (str — closed enum: `P0` / `P1` / empty), `jaccard_similarity_bucket` (str — closed enum: `<=0.3` / `0.3-0.5` / `0.5-0.8` / `>0.8` / empty; raw float forbidden per Sec MF-3), `human_triage_grace_h` (int ≥0 — hours remaining in 24h grace window per R1 S-TDE-4; 0 = grace expired = closes-as-advisory; CEO_PAIR_RAIL_HUMAN_TRIAGE_HOURS env override), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget this invocation ran under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Purpose is §4(i): before this field a case F produced by a sub-floor `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S` export was byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage, which made the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented kill-switch. Encoding is load-bearing, not stylistic: a float in an HMAC-covered field is rejected by `_lib/canonical_json.py` and the spool writer then DROPS THE WHOLE EVENT with only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — for this action that would manufacture the very /ceo-boot liveness deficit `review_id` exists to disprove), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline HMAC-chain invariant. PLAN-081 Phase 3 (S100 ceremony 2026-05-10) — emitted by `.claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:_decide_with_matrix()` once per Pair-Rail PreToolUse evaluation that reaches the matrix arm (write tool + L3+ path + no sentinel bypass). Source action for `fp_rate_30d` and `disagreement_rate_30d` predicate aggregators. ADR-107 + ADR-108 ACCEPTED gate. Sec MF-3 invariant: NEVER persist raw Codex review body / proposed-content / file path. Registered with `KERNEL_OVERRIDE` bypass since `audit_emit.py` is in `_KERNEL_PATHS`. |
.claude/plans/PLAN-162/ceremony-2-staged/amend2-pair-rail.patch:842: | `pair_rail_promotion` (v2.23) | `action`, `run_id` (str ≤36 — UUID hex), `verdict` (str — closed enum: `PASS` / `PASS_AFTER_RETRY` / `TRIAGE` / `FAIL`), `corpus_n` (int ≥0), `corpus_manifest_sha` (str — 16-hex prefix), `catch_rate_num` (int ≥0), `catch_rate_den` (int ≥1), `fp_rate_bucket` (str — closed enum: `<=15%` / `15-30%` / `>30%` / empty), `schema_adherence_pct_bucket` (str — closed enum: `100%` / `95-99%` / `<95%` / empty), `rubric_gap_pp_bucket` (str — closed enum: `<=0pp` / `0-5pp` / `5-10pp` / `>10pp` / empty), `codex_cli_version` (str ≤32), `python_version` (str ≤16), `git_head_sha_prefix` (str — 12-hex prefix), `pass_2_retry_used` (bool), `manual_triage` (bool), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline HMAC-chain invariant. PLAN-081 Phase 4 (S100 ceremony 2026-05-10) — emitted by `.claude/scripts/run-promotion-gate.py` at end of each locked-corpus promotion-gate run. Source for `u7_rubric_gap_pp` predicate aggregator. ADR-111 ACCEPTED gate. Sec MF-3 invariant: NEVER persist raw fixture content / Codex review body / proposed-content. Registered with `KERNEL_OVERRIDE` bypass. |
.claude/plans/PLAN-162/ceremony-2-staged/amend2-pair-rail.patch:858:+| v2.55 | ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6 (pair-rail timeout recalibration 120/150 → 180/210 s, S291 ceremony 2026-08-03) — NO new action (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` stays 324) and no new allowlist. ONE new bounded field `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the invocation ran under) added to the EXISTING `pair_rail_case` AND `pair_rail_review_expected` allowlists, coerced in both typed wrappers AND both `emit_generic` dispatch branches (never `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`). Motivation is the §4(i) named residual: no event recorded the effective budget, so a session exporting `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S=5` produced a case F byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage — making the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE` kill-switch, which emits its own loud event. A minimum floor on the knob stays DEFERRED (changing a documented knob's semantics is a new contract, AMEND-1 consensus item 2), but the incentive gradient is no longer inverted and the next amendment's historical series is no longer born ambiguous. **Encoding is normative, not stylistic:** MILLISECONDS as an int, NOT the float seconds the amendment prose names — `_lib/canonical_json.py` rejects floats in HMAC-covered fields, and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb, which on these two actions would manufacture the exact /ceo-boot S254 liveness deficit they exist to measure. Same encoding + rationale as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` (PLAN-081 Phase 2, Codex iter 1 P0-1). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. | *(1 new bounded int field on 2 existing actions; no new actions, no new allowlists; shared coercion `_coerce_pair_rail_timeout_ms` + bound `_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX` in `audit_emit.py`)* |
