.claude/plans/PLAN-164/review/codex-rail-r4.md:6:| R3 N2 — reverted ceremony cannot anchor | UNIT-CLOSED, END-TO-END OPEN | The staged resolver rejects a file-pointed reverted SHA and skips reverted fallback candidates ([land-plan163-pin.sh:125](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:125), [land-plan163-pin.sh:153](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:153), [land-plan163-pin.sh:157](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:157)). But that resolver is itself landed in—and therefore removed by reverting—the ceremony. |
.claude/plans/PLAN-164/review/codex-rail-r1.md:4:   `resolve_anchor` accepts any subject containing either sentinel marker and its fallback selects the newest matching commit ([land-plan163-pin.sh:106](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:106), [land-plan163-pin.sh:114](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:114), [land-plan163-pin.sh:119](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:119)). The instructed closeout subject reuses `[SENT-PLAN164-RAIL]` ([land-plan164-rail.sh:529](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/land-plan164-rail.sh:529)). Therefore a pointer changed to the closeout SHA passes validation, and an absent anchor file automatically falls back to that newer commit. This moves the audit cutoff forward and can launder events between the ceremony and closeout, contrary to the intended ceremony-commit anchor.
