.claude/skills/domains/cpp/skills/cpp-build-systems/SKILL.md:174:# Git form: full commit SHA only. A tag can be re-pointed; a SHA cannot.
.claude/plans/PLAN-164/review/codex-rail-r2.md:7:| Codex R1-1 — closeout could become anchor | CLOSED | Closeout subject no longer contains the sentinel tag ([land-plan164-rail.sh:548](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/land-plan164-rail.sh:548)); anchor SHA must equal a canonical commit ([land-plan163-pin.sh:113](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:113), [land-plan163-pin.sh:122](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:122)). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-164/review/codex-rail-r2.md:20:1. **HIGH — Canonical-oldest creates a post-revert recovery deadlock.** After a revert, the original tagged commit remains in history, so the real ceremony refuses to rerun ([land-plan164-rail.sh:192](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/land-plan164-rail.sh:192)). Even if that guard were bypassed, a new ceremony SHA written into the anchor would be rejected because `resolve_anchor` accepts only the oldest tag bearer ([land-plan163-pin.sh:106](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:106), [land-plan163-pin.sh:122](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:122)). This directly contradicts the printed rollback instruction to “re-run the ceremony” after reverting ([land-plan164-rail.sh:567](/Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/land-plan164-rail.sh:567)).
.claude/skills/domains/cpp/skills/cpp-testing/SKILL.md:218:  URL https://github.com/google/googletest/archive/refs/tags/${GTEST_TAG}.zip
.claude/plans/PLAN-164/review/codex-rail-r3.md:37:   `resolve_anchor` validates commit existence and subject suffix only; it never rejects a ceremony SHA that a later commit reverted ([land-plan163-pin.sh:134](</Users/joaocanhada/canhada-labs/ceo-orchestration/.claude/plans/PLAN-164/staged/rail-pack/.claude/plans/PLAN-163/land-plan163-pin.sh:134>)). Because the closeout—and therefore its pointer—survives the prescribed rollback, `--gate-v2` can continue anchoring on the reverted ceremony until recovery occurs. This should fail closed during the rollback window.
