.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-r1/verdict-r1.txt:2:   **FILE:LINE:** `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml:41`, `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml:55`, `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml:276`; `.github/workflows/release.yml:13`, `.github/workflows/release.yml:231`, `.github/workflows/release.yml:647`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-r1/verdict-r1.txt:3:   **Failure scenario:** Push `v1.3.0`; `release.yml` and `npm-publish.yml` start independently. The release gate can reject the 24-hour hold, GPG signature, tests, or GA-specific verdict, while an approved `production-npm` job proceeds directly to `npm publish`. The driver incorrectly says `release.yml` itself publishes npm at `.claude/scripts/local/release-v1-2-0.sh:515`. The rejected version is then irreversibly public.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-r1/verdict-r1.txt:4:   **Minimal fix:** Put the npm publish job in `release.yml` with `needs: release-gate`, retaining the protected environment; alternatively trigger it only from a successful Release workflow and bind the exact tag SHA.
