  1218	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1219	# PLAN162_FIX_1 — the gpg subprocess is bounded by the REMAINING budget
  1220	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1221	# Codex pair-rail P1 (S292) against this patch, staged:
  1222	#
  1223	#   "Bound GPG verification by the remaining hook budget. When gpg or
  1224	#   gpg-agent stalls, this call can block for 15 seconds although the
  1225	#   hook is registered for 5 seconds and the new internal deadline is 4
  1226	#   seconds. Because the deadline is checked only between sentinel
  1227	#   iterations, the harness can kill the process before it emits the
  1228	#   intended fail-closed decision, recreating the silent fail-open that
  1229	#   ADR-164-AMEND-1 §3 explicitly says the patch prevents."
  1230	#
  1231	# The deadline above is POLLED: read at the top of the sentinel loops, it
  1232	# can only bound work that happens BETWEEN iterations. One
  1233	# ``verify_detached`` at the library default (``timeout=15.0``,
  1234	# ``_lib/gpg_verify.py``) is 3x the entire registration — the poll never
  1235	# gets its turn, the harness kills a hook that has emitted NOTHING, and
  1236	# "no decision" is indistinguishable from allow. ADR-164-AMEND-1 §3 D2
  1237	# already states the intended behaviour ("per-verify subprocess timeout
  1238	# bounded by remaining budget"); this is the code that makes the text
  1239	# true.
  1240	#
  1241	# Two constants, both about EMITTING rather than about gpg:
  1242	#
  1243	#   * ``_GPG_EMIT_MARGIN_S`` — wall time reserved AFTER gpg returns so the
  1244	#     rest of the decision plus the JSON emit still fit inside the
  1245	#     internal deadline. A verification bounded to land exactly ON the
  1246	#     deadline would merely have moved the kill.
  1247	#   * ``_GPG_MIN_SPAWN_S`` — the floor below which spawning is pointless:
  1248	#     a fork we cannot afford to wait out cannot tell "bad signature"
  1249	#     from "slow agent", so it must not start at all.
  1250	#
  1251	# Their sum must stay well under ``_HOOK_WALL_BUDGET_S``, or the FIRST
  1252	# sentinel of a fresh invocation could never be verified — self-DoS with
  1253	# the Owner's signature in hand, the C3 class. Pinned by
  1254	# ``test_control_gpg_bound_constants_leave_room_for_a_first_verify``.
  1255	_GPG_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_CAP_S = 15.0  # the historical _lib.gpg_verify default
